~ intro
Mooner: Woah Woah! Calm down!
Mooner: How are you feeling, you hit your head pretty hard there
Mooner: Huh you don’t remember anything!?!?!
Mooner: Do you at least remember your name?
do ask_name()
You: {{player_name}}
Mooner: …
Mooner: Ok at least some of your memories aren’t damaged
Mooner: …
Mooner: Uhhh I guess I have to reintroduce myself
Mooner: I’m Walpurgisnacht but you can call me Mooner
Mooner: I’m from the moon and we were traveling back to my home to do some research
Mooner: …
Mooner: Well maybe for some repairs too
Mooner: Your antenna is broken!
Mooner: Well you still remember how to slingshot right?
- No (tutorial)
	Mooner: Oh no....
	Mooner: Well It’s alright there’s a book here somewhere
	Mooner: …
	Mooner: …
	Mooner: Here it is!
	Mooner: …
	Mooner: You can’t read it?
	Mooner: Lemme read it for you
	Mooner: “To prepare for slingshot, you must prepare an accurate delta-v”
	Mooner: Oh Delta-V! You remember that don’t you?
	Mooner: Oh…You don’t…
	Mooner: Well Delta-V is like the change in speed the spacecraft should get
	Mooner: From how much fuel is used you know…
	Mooner: Seems easy enough
	Mooner: Go ahead, try it out!
	Mooner: I don’t have the hands to help you here
	Mooner: You can ask me again if you need to!
	do tutorial_delta_v()
	Mooner: Hey! Memory or not, you still got it!
	Mooner: I think…?
	Mooner: Now then before we launch we need to get the research in.
	Mooner: It’s in the paper somewhere
	Mooner: “Next is your research panel,
	Mooner: Your rocket does not supply enough power for all research equipment.
	Mooner: Therefore before slingshot you must choose machines you wish to power for your research”
	Mooner: …
	Mooner: Seems pretty easy!
	Mooner: You got that right?
	Mooner: You can ask me again if you need to!
	do tutorial_research()
	Mooner: Choosing the same choices as before…
	Mooner: I guess your preferences are the same!
	Mooner: Then come on!
	Mooner: Let’s blast off!
	=> blast_off
- Yes (reach for the stars)
	Mooner: Alright, then show me what you’ve got!
	do open_planner()
	Mooner: Set up the rocket however you like.
	Mooner: Then come on! Let’s blast off!
	=> blast_off

~ blast_off
do wait_for_launch()
=> landing

~ landing
Mooner: I’ll go ask for some moonians to fix the antenna!
Mooner: You can try to learn the machines and do some of the research!
Mooner: There should be drawings on how to use each machine!
Mooner: I’ll be back once you’ve finished all the research!
Mooner: Make sure you have plenty of food, water and oxygen!
Mooner: I’ll be back!
do mooner_leave()
=> END

~ return_home
Mooner: I’m back!
Mooner: It seems that you finished!
Mooner: Nice one!
Mooner: Let’s go back to Earth!
do unlock_return()
=> END

~ hint_delta_v
Mooner: Delta-V is like the change in speed the spacecraft should get, from how much fuel is used.
Mooner: Try raising it until it is enough to reach the Moon!
=> END

~ hint_research
Mooner: The paper says your rocket does not supply enough power for all the research equipment.
Mooner: So choose the machines you want to power, and keep the payload under your power!
=> END
